{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03539",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.78,
      "end_seconds": 6.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.4,
      "end_seconds": 12.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.03,
      "end_seconds": 25.72,
      "duration_seconds": 11.69,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come. Actually, we came because of an itchy red rash on the chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.15,
      "end_seconds": 28.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.87,
      "end_seconds": 34.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I'd say about a month, you know, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 35.41,
      "end_seconds": 39.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Hm, I'd say more like about two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.82,
      "end_seconds": 45.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.99,
      "end_seconds": 49.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Yeah, um, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.67,
      "end_seconds": 53.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.39,
      "end_seconds": 55.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.67,
      "end_seconds": 60.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.31,
      "end_seconds": 67.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get spreading over a week as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.05,
      "end_seconds": 74.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 74.58,
      "end_seconds": 79.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.01,
      "end_seconds": 87.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.62,
      "end_seconds": 96.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything. How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.84,
      "end_seconds": 99.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.34,
      "end_seconds": 104.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Have you had blistering, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.75,
      "end_seconds": 108.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no blistering."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.12,
      "end_seconds": 113.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Sure. Right, any mouth sores, breathing difficulty or facial swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.6,
      "end_seconds": 129.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.98,
      "text": "No, no mouth sores, no breathing difficulty, no facial swelling. I did have a mild temperature at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.67,
      "end_seconds": 135.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.66,
      "end_seconds": 139.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.28,
      "end_seconds": 144.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.03,
      "end_seconds": 152.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Let me think, my father had bowel cancer. Ah, my cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.2,
      "end_seconds": 156.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.33,
      "end_seconds": 168.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "Febuxostat. I take it 80 milligrams, once a day. Seretide inhaler. I take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.6,
      "end_seconds": 172.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "How long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.34,
      "end_seconds": 176.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "About nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.74,
      "end_seconds": 187.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Right, now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.4,
      "end_seconds": 203.17,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.65,
      "end_seconds": 207.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.42,
      "end_seconds": 218.84,
      "duration_seconds": 10.42,
      "text": "I had my septum straightened in my thirties. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.8,
      "end_seconds": 223.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.03,
      "end_seconds": 234.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.66,
      "end_seconds": 239.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.52,
      "end_seconds": 245.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "I've got gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.89,
      "end_seconds": 250.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.68,
      "end_seconds": 252.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Yes, asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.23,
      "end_seconds": 255.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 256.78,
      "end_seconds": 267.96,
      "duration_seconds": 11.18,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pressure 117 over 69, respiratory rate 15, heart rate 84. Temp 36.5 degrees, oxygen saturation is 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.29,
      "end_seconds": 271.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.99,
      "end_seconds": 276.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.53,
      "end_seconds": 280.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.73,
      "end_seconds": 284.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Okay, I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.82,
      "end_seconds": 308.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "There is a fine pink rash across the chest and arms, with no blistering and the mouth is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.87,
      "end_seconds": 316.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.64,
      "end_seconds": 352.9,
      "duration_seconds": 21.26,
      "text": "Blood tests is what I'd like next, for drug rash. The treatment will be cetirizine, 10 milligrams, once a day, one week. You take it by mouth. That's for itch. Please stop the allopurinol and don't restart it until we've spoken to the clinic. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.69,
      "end_seconds": 356.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}